UPDATE lessons SET title='Year 3, Week 24, Lesson 2: Length investigation: our school grounds', data=json_patch(data,'{"child_mission":"A length investigation of school/home grounds plans what to measure, chooses units, records results and compares findings.","coming_soon":null,"duration_minutes":55,"evidence_instructions":"Save the independent response, specific revisions and both short-answer explanations; record oral evidence for speaking tasks.","explicit_teaching":null,"extension":"Apply the same method to a larger number or a new context, then compare two solution paths for accuracy.","follow_up_challenges":null,"guided_practice":"PRACTISE BEFORE READING THE FEEDBACK\nDesign measures for: a doorway height; a table length; a short outdoor path. Choose units.\n\nFEEDBACK\nHeight/path often m or cm; table often cm; justify each choice.\n\nWATCH FOR\nMeasuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place.","hoard_words":null,"independent_task":"INDEPENDENT EVIDENCE\nComplete a grounds/home length investigation: at least five measures, unit choices, a results table and three comparison sentences. Note one measurement challenge.\n\nWrite a short reflection naming one step you corrected and why.","interactive_activities":null,"learning_area":"Mathematics","learning_intention":"A length investigation of school/home grounds plans what to measure, chooses units, records results and compares findings.","lesson_number":2,"lesson_role":"Strategies","materials":["Paper or typed answer space","Pencil","Optional: place-value chart or number line"],"offline_alternative":"Use paper and pencil to complete the original task, then retain a photograph or short parent observation as evidence.","outcome_codes":["MA2-GM-01"],"parent_notes":"Parent: Marking guidance for the independent task: Complete a grounds/home length investigation: at least five measures, unit choices, a results table and three comparison sentences. Note one measurement challenge. Accept equivalent original responses that show the same skill.\n\nParent: Written model 1: Sample: new numbers solved with visible working for investigation; key places/values named. Do not award marks for retyping the model.\n\nParent: Written model 2: Sample misconception: Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place.. Correction uses Height/path often m or cm;. Why: restores accurate investigation.\n\nParent: Likely misconception: Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place. Keep sample answers out of the child role.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 1: Solve one fresh problem that uses investigation with different numbers from the worked model. Show working and name the places or values that matter.\n\nParent: Short-answer focus 2: Describe one likely mistake with investigation, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.\n\nParent: Marking notes: Accept any mathematically valid solution that uses new numbers, shows working for investigation, and names places/values. Reject copied model numbers. / Accept a named misconception about investigation, corrected working, and a method reason. Reject vague “I was wrong” with no repair..","pass":1,"pass_mark":0.9,"planner_fields":null,"planner_intro":null,"planner_title":null,"printable_resource":null,"quiz":[{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"This matches the taught method for investigation. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Height/path often m or cm","Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place","A claim that names no evidence from the lesson material","A method that skips the key step taught in this lesson"],"question":"Design measures for: a doorway height; a table length; a short outdoor path. Choose units. Which response is most accurate?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"This is the misconception to avoid for investigation; the other choices align with the lesson method. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["A length investigation of school/home grounds plans what to measure, chooses units, records results and compares","Height/path often m or cm","Careful use of grounds and explain why it matters with clear evidence","Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place"],"question":"Which statement is a common mistake when working with investigation?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Understanding is shown by new evidence and a named grounds and explain why it matters, not by copying the model. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place","Name grounds and explain why it matters only, without linking it to investigation","Apply investigation to new material and name the grounds and explain why it matters used","Repeat the worked example wording with no new evidence"],"question":"Which response best applies investigation with new evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"Mathematics answers need labelled working tied to place value, quantity or the asked operation. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Change digits to look neater without checking place value","Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place","Show each place, value or step and say why that step is valid","Write only a final number with no working"],"question":"Which working best supports a correct answer for this lesson on investigation?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":2,"explanation":"The correct statement applies the taught investigation method; the others break place value, units or the asked quantity. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Read 24 from left to right as ones only, ignoring place value","Ignore units and treat 24 and 6 as interchangeable","Height/path often m or cm","Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place"],"question":"Using the method for investigation, which statement is true?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Disagreement is resolved by checking places, operations and the question focus, not by blending answers. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Pick the longer-looking working automatically","Delete units so the answers appear to match","Average the two answers without checking either","Recheck places, operations and whether the question asked for the quantity you computed"],"question":"If two methods disagree on a investigation problem with numbers such as 24 and 6, what should you check first?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Transfer requires new numbers with the same mathematical method and a named reason. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Use the same investigation method on new numbers and name the places or values that matter","Retype the worked model numbers 24 and 6 as the answer","Change only handwriting and keep the same numbers","Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place"],"question":"Solve a fresh investigation problem that uses different numbers from the worked model and explain one key step.?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Recognising the warned misconception protects accuracy on new problems. The other choices miss a key step or use a common mistake.","options":["Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place","A length investigation of school/home grounds plans what to measure, chooses units, records results and compares","Height/path often m or cm","Label units when comparing 24 with 6"],"question":"Which error is the lesson warning against for investigation?","type":"multiple_choice"},{"explanation":"Independent evidence on new material demonstrates the skill; copying the model does not.","marking_guide":"Accept any mathematically valid solution that uses new numbers, shows working for investigation, and names places/values. Reject copied model numbers.","question":"Solve one fresh problem that uses investigation with different numbers from the worked model. Show working and name the places or values that matter.","sample_answer":"Sample: new numbers solved with visible working for investigation; key places/values named. Do not award marks for retyping the model.","type":"short_answer"},{"explanation":"A useful correction changes the inaccurate idea or method and explains why.","marking_guide":"Accept a named misconception about investigation, corrected working, and a method reason. Reject vague “I was wrong” with no repair.","question":"Describe one likely mistake with investigation, show corrected working, and say why the correction works.","sample_answer":"Sample misconception: Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place.. Correction uses Height/path often m or cm;. Why: restores accurate investigation.","type":"short_answer"}],"resources":null,"response_prompt":"Include your independent working and reflection, with reasons where requested.","review_status":"unreviewed","seed_key":"s2-mat-y3-w24-l2","sort_activity":null,"source_note":"Proposed Stage 2 NESA mathematics alignment using verified outcome code wording where recorded in lesson-pipeline/sources; content-point mapping remains pending.","spelling":null,"spelling_focus":null,"stage":"S2","stage_hints":{"accept":["Today you will practise investigation.","Read the mission before you start calculating.","Keep the place or unit you are working with in view."],"guided":["Attempt the guided prompt without looking ahead.","Afterwards, compare your working with the feedback.","Adjust anything that does not match the method."],"learn":["Study how the first demonstration is built.","Point to the place or distance that carries the method.","Then write the reason without copying every sentence."],"quiz":["Read every option before you choose.","Eliminate answers that ignore place value or working.","Prefer accurate method over a guess that merely looks neat."],"submit":["Confirm that your working and reason are both present.","Proofread digits, places and operation signs.","Make sure the final evidence matches the lesson purpose."],"teach0":["Read the stage title and find the worked model.","Name one exact place, value or distance before you decide.","Try the small prompt before opening the comparison."],"teach1":["Return to the model and list the key numbers.","Say what each number represents in the method.","A final answer alone is weaker than labelled working."],"teach2":["Compare a weak attempt with stronger working.","Change the value or method, not only how neat it looks.","Name the mistake you are repairing."],"teach3":["Choose fresh numbers that still use the same skill.","Write one reason in your own words.","Do not retype the worked model as your answer."],"write":["Follow every part of the independent instructions.","Include original working and a short reason.","Save work that shows the skill on new numbers."]},"subject":"Measurement and Space","success_criteria":["I can use investigation with a specific example from this lesson.","I can identify grounds and explain why it matters.","I can practise plan independently on a new prompt.","I can notice record needs and correct a likely mistake."],"suspense_builder":null,"teach_steps":[{"check":{"correct_index":3,"explanation":"A length investigation of school/home grounds plans what to measure, chooses units, records results and compares findings.","options":["A calculation unrelated to the numbers given","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no working","A length investigation of school/home grounds plans what to measure, chooses units, records results and compares"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about investigation with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nPlan: measure path width in cm, garden length in m, step distance roughly in m. Record in a table and compare which is longest.\n\nTRY FIRST\nDesign measures for: a doorway height; a table length; a short outdoor path. Choose units.\n\nFEEDBACK\nHeight/path often m or cm; table often cm; justify each choice.","explain":"A length investigation of school/home grounds plans what to measure, chooses units, records results and compares findings.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Understand and model","visual":[{"alt":"Investigation plan for grounds lengths.","caption":"A table keeps results organised.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Plan</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">what to measure</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Units</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">cm or m chosen</text></g></svg>"}],"visual_before":[{"episode":{"scenes":[{"bg":"room","lines":[{"text":"I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.","who":"pip"},{"text":"Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.","who":"juno"},{"text":"I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.","who":"pip"},{"pause_after":true,"text":"Pause here. Use this model: Plan: measure path width in cm, garden length in m, step distance roughly in m. Record in a table and compare which is l Then write your own working.","who":"juno"}]}],"title":"Talk through the first model","transcript":"Pip: I can see the example, but I am not sure which number or place matters most.\nJuno: Name the places, values or distances that carry the method before you decide.\nPip: I will try the prompt myself, then compare with the feedback.\nJuno: Pause here. Use this model: Plan: measure path width in cm, garden length in m, step distance roughly in m. Record in a table and compare which is l Then write your own working."}}]},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid.","options":["Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no working"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about investigation with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nPlan: measure path width in cm, garden length in m, step distance roughly in m. Record in a table and compare which is longest. Look at each number, place or distance that carries the method.\n\nTRY FIRST\nWrite the key numbers from the model and say what each one represents in the method.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe most useful working names the quantities and the reason for each step, not only the final answer.","explain":"Make the method visible: name the values, places or steps you used and say why that step is valid.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Writing only the final answer without working does not show the method. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Show the working","visual":[{"alt":"Comparison sentences from recorded measures.","caption":"Plan before measuring.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Compare</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">which is longest</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Challenge</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">note one difficulty</text></g></svg>"}]},{"check":{"correct_index":1,"explanation":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison.","options":["An answer copied without understanding","Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison","A guess with no working","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about investigation with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nMeasuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place. Here is a more productive model: Plan: measure path width in cm, garden length in m, step distance roughly in m. Record in a table and compare which is longest.\n\nTRY FIRST\nDescribe why the warned-against approach gives the wrong value or meaning, then write corrected working.\n\nFEEDBACK\nHeight/path often m or cm; table often cm; justify each choice.","explain":"Use an intentionally incorrect attempt as a comparison. Name its specific mathematical error, then show the corrected working.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Changing the answer without repairing the method does not fix the error. Measuring without a recording plan loses which number belongs to which place. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Test a misconception"},{"check":{"correct_index":0,"explanation":"Use the method on new numbers or a new context, not a copy of the worked example.","options":["Use the method on new numbers or a new context, not a copy of the worked example","A calculation unrelated to the numbers given","An answer copied without understanding","A guess with no working"],"question":"Which choice best applies this lesson idea about investigation with clear evidence?","type":"multiple_choice"},"example":"WORKED MODEL\nA length investigation of school/home grounds plans what to measure, chooses units, records results and compares findings. Now choose different numbers to show you can transfer the method.\n\nTRY FIRST\nSolve one fresh problem that uses the same skill and write a short reason for your answer.\n\nFEEDBACK\nThe new problem should use the same method as the model, but contain different numbers.","explain":"Use the method on new numbers or a new context, not a copy of the worked example. Review accuracy and units or places.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS\nThis helps the learner choose methods based on place value, quantity and accurate working, rather than guessing digits by shape alone. Keep every step justified.\n\nHOW TO WORK\nRead the worked example and name the places, values or distances that carry the method. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Compare your working with the feedback: did you use the same skill and show your reasoning? If a digit or place is uncertain, identify what would have to be regrouped or counted again. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than writing a longer answer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new numbers. Correct the value or method, not just the appearance of the digits.","title":"Transfer to a new problem"}],"title":"Year 3, Week 24, Lesson 2: Length investigation: our school grounds","unit_number":6,"unit_title":"Length and perimeter","week":24,"week_in_unit":4,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nPlan: measure path width in cm, garden length in m, step distance roughly in m. Record in a table and compare which is longest.\n\nWrite what makes this example accurate, naming the places, values or distances used.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Investigation plan for grounds lengths.","caption":"A table keeps results organised.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14